{
  "id": "m8-b2",
  "title": "Reverse the Coolant Line",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "story": "The coolant valves are a linked list, and the pump needs them in the opposite order. Build the list **in input order** (add each node at the tail), then **reverse the list itself** by re-pointing the nodes. Don't just print it backwards.\n\nInput: `n` (0–1000), then n whole numbers.\n\nOutput: the reversed list in the form `3 -> 2 -> 1 -> NULL`. An empty list prints `NULL`.\n\n`print_list` and `free_list` are written for you; finish `append` and `reverse`.",
  "starter": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct Node {\n    int value;\n    struct Node *next;\n} Node;\n\n// Add value at the END of the list; return the (possibly new) head.\nNode *append(Node *head, int value) {\n    return head;\n}\n\n// Reverse the list by re-pointing each node's next; return the new head.\nNode *reverse(Node *head) {\n    return head;\n}\n\nvoid print_list(Node *head) {\n    for (Node *p = head; p != NULL; p = p->next) printf(\"%d -> \", p->value);\n    printf(\"NULL\\n\");\n}\n\nvoid free_list(Node *head) {\n    while (head != NULL) {\n        Node *next = head->next;\n        free(head);\n        head = next;\n    }\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    Node *head = NULL;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int v;\n        scanf(\"%d\", &v);\n        head = append(head, v);\n    }\n    head = reverse(head);\n    print_list(head);\n    free_list(head);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
  "tests": [
